{%- comment -%}
  Animated figure for Structured-Data Foundation Models on /research/: a table fills in row by row,
  then each query row attends to the labelled context rows (arcs, thicker = more attention) and its y is predicted.
  Square size encodes the value. Animations: .rs-* in _sass/_research.scss.
{%- endcomment -%}
<figure class="research-fig">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 360 360"
    role="img"
    aria-label="A data table with four feature columns and a target column y. Four labelled context rows appear, then two query rows whose y is unknown. Each query row reaches back to the context labels with blue arcs, thicker where it attends more, and its prediction fills in blue in one pass"
  >
    <g font-family="Lato, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" font-weight="700" font-size="14" fill="#222222" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="58" y="26">x₁</text>
      <text x="108" y="26">x₂</text>
      <text x="158" y="26">x₃</text>
      <text x="208" y="26">x₄</text>
      <text x="274" y="26">y</text>
    </g>
    <path d="M36 34H296" stroke="#222222" stroke-width="1.5"></path>
    <g class="rs-cycle">
      <g font-family="Lato, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" font-weight="700" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1.5" fill="#555555" text-anchor="middle">
        <text x="18" y="137" transform="rotate(-90 18 137)">CONTEXT</text>
        <text x="18" y="301" transform="rotate(-90 18 301)" fill="#1772d0">QUERY</text>
      </g>
      <path d="M28 40V234M28 254V348" stroke="#bbbbbb" stroke-width="2"></path>
      <path d="M36 244H296" stroke="#bbbbbb" stroke-width="1"></path>
